WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.989 --> 00:00:19.051
Mary went to fetch Ben Weatherstaff and bring him into the garden to meet Colin.

2
00:00:20.251 --> 00:00:23.653
The main thing to remember, she told him, was that Colin was getting well.

3
00:00:24.853 --> 00:00:26.374
The garden was making him well.

4
00:00:27.635 --> 00:00:30.436
No one needed to remind him about lumps or dying.

5
00:00:31.976 --> 00:00:35.598
Meanwhile Colin was determined to be standing when Ben entered the garden.

6
00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:39.440
"I'm going to walk to that tree," he said to Dickon.

7
00:00:40.661 --> 00:00:43.843
"I can lean against it if I get tired, but I'll still be standing."

8
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:45.643
Dickon nodded.

9
00:00:45.663 --> 00:00:49.345
"I told you that you could stand as soon as you stopped being afraid."

10
00:00:49.365 --> 00:00:51.947
"I'm not afraid anymore."

11
00:00:52.387 --> 00:00:53.808
Colin suddenly thought of something.

12
00:00:53.828 --> 00:00:57.230
"Are you making some magic that's helping me stand?"

13
00:00:58.410 --> 00:00:59.131
Dickon grinned.

14
00:00:59.151 --> 00:01:01.212
"You're making that magic yourself.

15
00:01:02.536 --> 00:01:06.099
It's the same magic that makes these flowers work their way out of the dirt."

16
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.322
He touched a clump of crocuses with his foot.

17
00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.905
Just then Ben and Mary came through the door in the wall.

18
00:01:13.925 --> 00:01:19.070
"Look at me, Weatherstaff," ordered Colin, standing tall by the tree.

19
00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.211
"Am I a hunchback?

20
00:01:21.632 --> 00:01:22.773
Do I have crooked legs?"

21
00:01:24.194 --> 00:01:24.654
"No, sir."

22
00:01:24.674 --> 00:01:28.517
"Everyone thinks I'm going to die, but I'm not."

23
00:01:30.139 --> 00:01:31.500
Ben looked him up and down.

24
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.642
"You have too much spirit to die.

25
00:01:35.963 --> 00:01:38.585
I saw that when you put your feet on the ground in such a hurry.

26
00:01:39.846 --> 00:01:41.687
Now sit down and give me your orders."

27
00:01:42.948 --> 00:01:45.991
Dickon spread a blanket on the ground, and helped Colin to sit.

28
00:01:47.272 --> 00:01:48.773
The others gathered around him.

29
00:01:48.793 --> 00:01:52.496
"What work do you do in the gardens, Weatherstaff?"

30
00:01:52.956 --> 00:01:53.617
asked Colin.

31
00:01:53.637 --> 00:01:57.220
"Anything I'm told to do," replied Ben.

32
00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.642
"I still work here because your mother liked me."

33
00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:02.384
"My mother?"

34
00:02:02.772 --> 00:02:03.772
Colin looked around.

35
00:02:03.792 --> 00:02:06.573
"This was her garden, wasn't it?"

36
00:02:07.713 --> 00:02:09.794
"Yes, and she was very fond of it."

37
00:02:11.474 --> 00:02:13.815
"It's my garden now, and I'm fond of it too.

38
00:02:14.935 --> 00:02:17.676
I'm going to come here every day," announced Colin.

39
00:02:17.696 --> 00:02:19.997
"But it's to be a secret.

40
00:02:21.137 --> 00:02:24.038
Mary and Dickon have worked hard to make the garden come alive.

41
00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:29.079
I'll send for you sometimes to help, but you must come when no one can see you."

42
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:31.440
Ben smiled.

43
00:02:32.052 --> 00:02:34.053
"I've come here before and no one saw me."

44
00:02:35.273 --> 00:02:36.373
"What! When?"

45
00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:37.554
Colin asked.

46
00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:40.874
"The last time was about two years ago."

47
00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:43.035
"But how did you get in?

48
00:02:44.275 --> 00:02:46.796
No one knew where the key was buried," said Colin.

49
00:02:46.816 --> 00:02:49.457
"I came over the wall.

50
00:02:49.517 --> 00:02:52.698
But my aching joints have held me back these last two years.

51
00:02:53.898 --> 00:02:55.998
It'll be easier now that I can come through the door."

52
00:02:56.018 --> 00:02:58.999
"So you're the one who did the pruning!"

53
00:02:59.399 --> 00:02:59.999
cried Dickon.

54
00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:02.540
"Yes," said Ben.

55
00:03:03.661 --> 00:03:08.283
He turned to Colin and said softly, "Your mother was such a pretty, young thing.

56
00:03:09.844 --> 00:03:15.406
She said to me once, 'Ben, if I'm ever ill, or if I go away, you must take

57
00:03:15.466 --> 00:03:16.627
care of my roses.'

58
00:03:18.047 --> 00:03:22.909
When she did go away, the orders were that no one was ever to come near the garden."

59
00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.851
Ben paused to collect his emotions.

60
00:03:27.111 --> 00:03:32.250
Then he said in a strong voice, "But I came over the wall because she gave her orders

61
00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:36.392
first." "I'm glad you did," said Colin.

62
00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:38.934
"You will know how to keep our secret."

63
00:03:40.655 --> 00:03:44.557
Earlier in the afternoon, Mary had dropped her trowel on the ground where they were sitting.

64
00:03:45.837 --> 00:03:47.939
Now Colin reached out and picked it up.

65
00:03:49.219 --> 00:03:51.361
He drove the end of the trowel into the dirt.

66
00:03:51.381 --> 00:03:53.922
"You can do it!"

67
00:03:54.342 --> 00:03:55.403
Mary said to herself.

68
00:03:56.804 --> 00:04:00.461
Sure enough, Colin managed to turn a few trowels full of dirt.

69
00:04:02.082 --> 00:04:05.143
"You said you'd have me walking and digging," Colin said to Dickon.

70
00:04:05.163 --> 00:04:08.305
"I thought you were saying that just to please me.

71
00:04:09.485 --> 00:04:12.106
But here it's only the first day, and I've already walked.

72
00:04:12.506 --> 00:04:13.387
And now I'm digging!"

73
00:04:13.407 --> 00:04:16.608
"How would you like to plant something?"

74
00:04:17.068 --> 00:04:17.608
asked Ben.

75
00:04:17.628 --> 00:04:20.550
"I can get you a rose from the greenhouse."

76
00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.851
"Go and get it quickly!"

77
00:04:24.011 --> 00:04:28.398
Colin began to dig excitedly, but he wasn't strong enough to dig a very big hole.

78
00:04:29.919 --> 00:04:32.901
Ben hurried off to get the rose while Dickon made the hole deeper.

79
00:04:34.222 --> 00:04:36.864
Mary ran out of the garden to fetch a watering can.

80
00:04:38.165 --> 00:04:40.266
Soon they were all gathered around Colin.

81
00:04:41.427 --> 00:04:43.028
Ben took the rose out of the pot.

82
00:04:44.309 --> 00:04:47.171
"I want to plant it before the sun sets," said Colin.

83
00:04:48.392 --> 00:04:50.933
His hands shook as he put the rose in the ground.

84
00:04:52.214 --> 00:04:54.356
He held it while Ben filled the hole with dirt.

85
00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:56.761
"It's planted!"

86
00:04:57.181 --> 00:04:57.862
cried Colin.

87
00:04:57.882 --> 00:05:00.525
"And the sun is almost down.

88
00:05:00.985 --> 00:05:01.726
Help me up, Dickon.

89
00:05:02.947 --> 00:05:04.529
I want to be standing when it sets.

90
00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:06.651
That's part of the magic."

91
00:05:07.933 --> 00:05:09.294
Dickon helped him to his feet.

92
00:05:09.895 --> 00:05:12.137
It had been a strange and lovely afternoon.

93
00:05:13.378 --> 00:05:18.404
And as the sun slipped below the horizon, Colin stood smiling in the secret garden.
